ame>Ogasawara</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishigo-oka</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kadoya</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Daito</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Moriya</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Subcellular localization of Dna-initiation proteins of <italic>Bacillus subtilis</italic>: evidence that chromosome replication begins at either edge of the nucleoids</article-title><source>Mol. Microbiol.</source><year>2000</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>1037</fpage><lpage>1048</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10844689</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Farache</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McGovern</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ehrlich</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Polard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DnaB, DnaD and DnaI proteins are components of the <italic>Bacillus subtilis</italic> replication restart primosome</article-title><source>Mol. Microbiol.</source><year>2001</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11679082</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McGovern</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ehrlich</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Polard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early steps of <italic>Bacillus subtilis</italic> primosome assembly</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>2001</year><volume>276</volume><fpage>45818</fpage><lpage>45825</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11585815</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rokop</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Auchtung</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Grossman</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Control of DNA replication initiation by recruitment of an essential initiation protein to the membrane of <italic>Bacillus subtilis</italic></article-title><source>Mol. Microbiol.</source><year>2004</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>1757</fpage><lpage>1767</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15186423</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Turner</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Soultanas</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The <italic>Bacillus subtilis</italic> DnaD protein: a putative link between DNA remodeling and initiation of DNA replication</article-title><source>FEBS Lett.</source><year>2004</year><volume>577</volume><fpage>460</fpage><lpage>464</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15556628</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Velten</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McGovern</surname><given-